{"step_index":77,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-03T22:38:04Z","content":"Priyanshu,\n\nThe full analysis is in [manhwa_niche_analysis.md](file:///C:/Users/renu5/.gemini/antigravity/brain/294de91b-96ee-4dd8-a251-293eb7aa59a8/manhwa_niche_analysis.md).\n\nHere's the bottom line, no sugarcoating:\n\n**The number that should change your mind:** Manhwa Outpost â€” the BIGGEST channel in this niche with **405,000 subscribers** â€” makes **\\$1,045/month**. Not \\$10K. Not \\$5K. One thousand dollars. The algorithm moved on and left them behind.\n\nYou're looking at 1221Recap during its peak month and thinking that's normal. It's not. 71.7% of their entire lifetime views happened in the LAST MONTH ALONE. That's a spike, not a baseline.\n\n**My recommendation: Don't do it.** Three specific reasons:\n\n1. **You can't quality-check what AI writes** because you've never read a single manhwa. The audience will catch errors by episode 1.\n2. **You haven't monetized your existing channel yet.** Starting a harder channel doesn't fix the skills gap â€” it compounds it.\n3. **You're competing against content farms** (I proved this â€” multiple channels share identical descriptions, meaning they're the same operator running 3-5 channels at once).\n\n**What to do instead:** Get your existing channel to 1K subs first. Learn what actually works. Then apply those skills to a niche where you have real knowledge and the content isn't built on copyrighted material that can get DMCA'd overnight.\n\nIf you still want to explore this or any of your other ideas, I'm here. But I won't tell you this is a good bet when the data says otherwise."}
