{"step_index":102,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-03T23:19:32Z","content":"Priyanshu,\n\nYou were right to push on this. I ran `/find-skills` to search the open ecosystem, and there are specific modular skills built exactly for the production bottlenecks we discussed. \n\nHere is the **New Analysis** of what your fully automated tech stack looks like if we pull these in:\n\n### 1. The TTS Bottleneck (Solved)\nI found `aahl/skills@edge-tts`. This solves the text-to-speech problem. It connects directly to Microsoft Edge's high-quality neural voices via the terminal. We feed it the 50,000-word text file, and it handles the rate limits and audio generation in the background. Zero manual copying and pasting.\n\n### 2. The Video & Captions Bottleneck (Solved)\nI found `digitalsamba/claude-code-video-toolkit@ffmpeg` and a specific sub-skill `ffmpeg-captions-subtitles`. These allow me to write the commands that take your audio and your images, apply the vertical panning effect automatically, generate the transcription, and burn the captions directly onto the video.\n\n### 3. The Image Slicing Bottleneck (Solved)\nI found `revfactory/webtoon-harness@webtoon-panel-breakdown`. Manhwa are published as massive vertical strips. This skill detects the blank space between comic boxes and slices the long strip into individual video-sized panels automatically. *(You still need to use a bulk-downloader like HakuNeko to grab the raw chapters first, but this solves the editing nightmare).*\n\n### The Revised Time Reality (The Catch)\nIf we install and configure this stack, your manual production time drops from 3-4 hours down to **45-60 minutes per video**. You act entirely as a manager: you run the downloader, you prompt the script generation, and you trigger the FFmpeg skills to assemble it.\n\n**Here is the remaining problem that automation cannot fix:**\nYou still have zero knowledge of the source material. The AI script generator *will* hallucinate parts of the 50,000-word script. It will mix up character names and invent plot points because it is summarizing raw text without understanding the visual context. \n\nIf we build this highly efficient factory, it will produce videos extremely fast. But if the scripts are inaccurate, the manhwa audience will immediately drop off, killing your watch time and preventing the channel from growing. \n\nAre you willing to spend that 45-60 minutes actually reading a summary of the source manhwa so you can quality-check the AI's script before we render it? That is the only way this automated system actually makes money.","thinking":"**Synthesizing Automation Possibilities**\n\nOkay, I'm now synthesizing the automation possibilities. The user's query about integration has me focusing on how to assemble skills for a new analysis. Right now, I'm noting the potential of `aahl/skills@edge-tts`, for high-quality, free TTS voices, which seems like a good place to start.\n\n\n**Refining Assembly Strategies**\n\nOkay, I've refined the assembly strategies. I've got video assembly and captioning with `digitalsamba/claude-code-video-toolkit@ffmpeg` and `josiahsiegel/claude-plugin-marketplace@ffmpeg-captions

